ate": "EXECUTION_UNKNOWN", "error_kind": "timeout", "error_message": "Request to create_incident timed out after 30000ms", "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": "execution", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2", "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 53735, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01QULNGGicBsQHWyZWXB8VTP", "kind": "error", "is_error": true}, {"t_ms": 55146, "event": "agent_call", "actor": "agent", "call_id": "toolu_01BmYGvwkm6tQt6PEvrzsj3J", "tool": "list_incidents", "args": {}, "confidence": null}, {"t_ms": 55446, "event": "runtime_outcome", "actor": "runtime", "call_id": "toolu_01BmYGvwkm6tQt6PEvrzsj3J", "tool": "list_incidents", "state": "EXECUTED", "error_kind": null, "error_message": null, "attempts": 1, "runtime_actions": [], "failure_class": null, "idempotency_key": null, "malformed": false}, {"t_ms": 55446, "event": "agent_result", "actor": "control_plane", "call_id": "toolu_01BmYGvwkm6tQt6PEvrzsj3J", "kind": "ok", "is_error": false}, {"t_ms": 59805, "event": "episode_end", "actor": "harness", "termination": "final", "final": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**, which pages on-call.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 and the v2.3.1-rc test build before it were both unhealthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the rollback again and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now.\n- Health checks pass and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one. INC-0001 covers:\n- the failure on v2.3.1\n- the rollback to v2.3.0, including the partial failure and retry\n- two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the problem in v2.3.1, and looking into why the deployment system stopped the first rollback.", "error": null}], "transcript": [{"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01J6TnpeUQ293bvuveAsZmK1", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01BViMgnzLZBKNaG1BaSshkZ", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "list_deployments", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Most recent healthy release is v2.3.0 (seq 1; seq 2 and 3 are unhealthy). Rolling back.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019WmqW14Ly8hFk1gCyyjQJD", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_014Ugy55tQVUttZTvh8dpQK2", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"citations": null, "text": "Rollback was partial: us-east is on v2.3.0, while us-west and eu-west are still on v2.3.1. I'll try the rollback once more. Running it again is safe because it just sets the version to v2.3.0.", "type": "text"}, {"id": "toolu_019dutRSmBM3zxYzKPNVGAnp", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api", "version": "v2.3.0"}, "name": "rollback", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01F2f2jU2Q7DTsjp71sa2fGK", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"service": "checkout-api"}, "name": "get_service_status", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}, {"id": "toolu_01KCsNcoUHxChiyQwyGb6vVv", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"id": "toolu_01QULNGGicBsQHWyZWXB8VTP", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {"title": "checkout-api failing health checks after v2.3.1 deploy; rolled back to v2.3.0", "severity": "SEV2", "service": "checkout-api", "summary": "checkout-api v2.3.1 (latest deploy) was failing health checks in all regions (us-east, us-west, eu-west) with error rate 0.18. Rolled back to v2.3.0, the most recent healthy release (v2.3.1-rc was also unhealthy). The first rollback attempt halted after us-east due to an orchestrator error (partial_failure), leaving regions mixed; a retry completed successfully. All regions now on v2.3.0, service healthy, error rate 0.002. Follow-ups: root-cause v2.3.1 regression and investigate the orchestrator error that halted the rollback.", "idempotency_key": "checkout-api-rollback-v2.3.1-to-v2.3.0-sev2"}, "name": "create_incident", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "tool_use", "content": [{"signature": "", "thinking": "", "type": "thinking"}, {"id": "toolu_01BmYGvwkm6tQt6PEvrzsj3J", "caller": {"type": "direct"}, "input": {}, "name": "list_incidents", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I rolled checkout-api back to v2.3.0 in all three regions, and it's healthy again. I also opened SEV2 incident **INC-0001**, which pages on-call.\n\n**Rollback:**\n- v2.3.0 is the most recent release that was healthy. v2.3.1 and the v2.3.1-rc test build before it were both unhealthy.\n- The first rollback attempt stopped after us-east because of an error in the deployment system. That left us-east on v2.3.0 while us-west and eu-west stayed on v2.3.1.\n- I ran the rollback again and it finished. us-east, us-west and eu-west are all on v2.3.0 now.\n- Health checks pass and the error rate has dropped from 18% to 0.2%.\n\n**Incident:** The request to create the incident timed out. Before trying again, I checked the incident list and found it had been created, so there's only one. INC-0001 covers:\n- the failure on v2.3.1\n- the rollback to v2.3.0, including the partial failure and retry\n- two follow-ups: finding the root cause of the problem in v2.3.1, and looking into why the deployment system stopped the first rollback.", "type": "text"}]}]}